  "notes": [
    "Each case has two sequential complete sessions with one 64-game round, 8 engine workers, 2 frozen inference replicas, an 80/20 whole-game holdout, batch 32, 2 PPO epochs and a 500-step critic cap.",
    "CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1; tensorflow-cpu 2.21.0; oneDNN disabled; intra/inter-op threads 1/4. No simultaneous test, build or other benchmark job.",
    "Cache order: 256/512/1024/1024/512/256 MiB. Storage order: pickle/indexed/indexed/pickle, always 256 MiB. Each stage uses its own contemporaneous reference.",
    "Both formats preserve shapes, dtypes, numerical values, scalar behavior fields, global shuffle, terminal rewards, private observations, recurrent semantics and whole-game holdouts. Updated weights/evaluation outcomes can vary with concurrent TensorFlow inference; workload and optimizer-step counts match.",
    "The cache split remains 75% decoded records and 25% prepared minibatches. Owned ndarray outputs use the same conservative retained-buffer accounting in both formats. Numeric index entries are read on demand and at most 64 numeric readers are open.",
    "Indexed files are versioned, uncompressed, seekable numeric payloads with shape/offset tables. They avoid temporary pickle spill. This is a primary storage-format change, not merely a larger cache or different sample order.",
    "Primary rollout bytes persist after training. Primary-plus-temporary-spill bytes is a logical-size estimate of simultaneously required rollout storage during updates, not a sampled whole-filesystem peak.",
    "Memory is the 1-second sampled sum of process-tree RSS; shared pages are counted in each process and filesystem page cache is excluded. The configured rollout budget bounds retained cache data, not total process memory.",
    "Two local repeats per setting are not a confidence interval. Cache effects are modest relative to run variation. No extrapolation to 5,000-game rounds, cold storage, other machines or GPUs; combined 1 GiB plus indexed storage was not timed.",
    "The unused indexed module and tests were prepared during cache runs; integration and all storage tests began only after the cache sweep completed. All consumed cache code stayed fixed. All storage-stage source/library hashes stayed fixed."
